[statement]
Reduced from a layered request over Alpine v3.24 (`main` and
`community`, 2026-11-11): `liferea`'s closure installed, `kdav-dev`
asked. The world is empty and `x`, unrelated, is requested, so every
installed package goes. `libpciaccess` and `zstd-libs` are needed
through names they provide at a version and are removed last: apk
removes `libpciaccess` first, whichever of `libdrm` and `libelf`, which
need them, the installed database lists first; with `libpciaccess` listed
before `zstd-libs` the orders agree. `musl` goes after both, which wait
on it, in the order of apk's table of names: `libpciaccess`'s own name
comes before `zstd-libs`'s names
(`installed/the-last-removals-go-in-the-order-of-apk-s-table-of-names`;
`reduced/lua5-4-s-freed-dependencies-are-removed-readline-first` is the
same shape).

[repository]
P:x
V:1-r0

[installed]
P:musl
V:1.2.6-r3
p:so:libc.musl-x86_64.so.1=1

P:zstd-libs
V:1.5.7-r2
D:so:libc.musl-x86_64.so.1
p:so:libzstd.so.1=1.5.7

P:libpciaccess
V:0.19-r0
D:so:libc.musl-x86_64.so.1
p:so:libpciaccess.so.0=0.11.1

P:libdrm
V:2.4.134-r0
D:so:libpciaccess.so.0

P:libelf
V:0.195-r0
D:so:libzstd.so.1

[request]
x

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove libdrm 2.4.134-r0
remove libelf 0.195-r0
install x 1-r0
remove libpciaccess 0.19-r0
remove zstd-libs 1.5.7-r2
remove musl 1.2.6-r3
